<section class="faq">
    <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

    <h3>Can I use these names in my novel or game?</h3>
    <p>Yes, completely free to use. Random combinations generated from syllable patterns are not copyrighted. If you accidentally generate a name that matches a well-known character or trademarked IP, that is a coincidence to watch out for, but the names themselves are yours to use.</p>

    <h3>How is this different from picking a name from a list?</h3>
    <p>Fixed lists run out quickly and produce repeats. This generator assembles names from phonetic components, so the potential combinations number in the millions and you rarely see the same name twice in a session. That makes it far more useful for bulk naming tasks like populating a city with NPCs.</p>

    <h3>Can I generate an elf name generator for D&D specifically?</h3>
    <p>Select the Elf style and neutral or your preferred gender lean. The elf names follow patterns consistent with high-fantasy D&D source material. They are not pulled from official D&D books, so they fit the style without infringing on any product content.</p>

    <h3>Does this store my generated names?</h3>
    <p>No. All generation happens in your browser. Nothing is sent to a server and nothing is saved. Refreshing the page clears the results.</p>
</section>

